      "side": 1,
      "message": "I think the issue is that you are changing the state, but not calling `test_reboot_to_next_step`. When you call `test_set_next_step`, it will set the flag for the next step, but won\u0027t actually advance it to the next step. The advancement to the next step happens after the reboot when your `test_run_step` function is called. \n\nI think you\u0027ll only need two steps:\n\n1. Check that TPM seed is zero, copy the fake value, check the fake value (The logic that you have in `test_tpm_seed_before_reboot`). Reboot.\n2. Check that TPM seed is zero (the logic that you have in `test_tpm_seed_after_reboot`). Reboot to `TEST_STATE_PASSED` or `TEST_STATE_FAILED` based on result of test.",
